Hi Alex,

Following the call, here is the integration picture in writing.

What we know:

- EPR: CarePoint 11.4. FHIR R4 read for Patient, Practitioner, Appointment and Schedule.
  Clinic letters are held as PDF documents in CarePoint and can be read as
  DocumentReference.
- Integration engine: Rhapsody-style engine run by our integration team (two people). It
  already sends HL7 v2 ADT messages (A04, A08, A40 merges) to eleven downstream systems.
- GP practices: 64 practices refer to us. They use two GP systems; both can send a
  referral as a structured message plus a PDF attachment.
- Notifications: we have an existing SMS contract with a gateway provider, 3.2p per
  message, and send about 40,000 reminders a month today from a home-grown script.

What nobody can know yet (please carry these as allowances):

- Whether CarePoint's FHIR API can write appointments back. If not, bookings go back
  through HL7 v2 SIU messages via the engine. CarePoint will only scope this after award.
- How many clinic codes are real. Between 300 and 900; it takes a walk-through with each
  service lead.

What is ours to decide or provide:

- A dedicated or shared CarePoint test system (we decide by end of November).
- Patient identity: national citizen login or our own accounts (December).
- Hosting: our Azure tenant or your hosted service. If it's our tenant, we provide the
  subscription, landing zone and network; if it's yours, it must be UK-hosted.
- Integration engine changes are done by our team, not yours; we need your message
  specifications at least six weeks before integration testing.
- Test patients: we will provide 200 synthetic test patients with appointment history.

Peak load: Monday mornings, when about 15,000 patients log in between 07:00 and 10:00.

Regards,
Owen Hartley
